# An operand that occurs twice: the checker treats each occurrence independently, so its interval cannot refute.
-- source.cue --
n: int32
-- target.cue --
z: 0
-- lens.cue --
v0_0: _
v1_0: {z: v0_0.n - v0_0.n}
-- out --
unknown
v1_0.z is an integer computed by v0_0.n - v0_0.n, in [-4294967295, 4294967295], which the checker cannot show within int64 and the target's 0 (an operand occurs more than once, and the checker treats each occurrence independently); bound the fields it reads (int32, >=0 & <=100) (rule unknown-bounds) @ lens.cue:2:11
